  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps` writes the smoothing ask as `G62 T<tol> P01 <0|1> P02 0`. `P01 0` is finish and `P01 1` is rough, from `PARAM SmoothingMode`. `P02 0` is the value that the control inserts for a `G62` with T only.\n- The dialect resolver has two new flags (`crates/post/src/post/heidenhain_profiles.rs`):\n  - `g62_mode` (`no` / `yes` / `option2`): the control takes `P01`. On the iTNC 530 340 49x and 606 42x, `P01` needs software option 2 (HSC machining). The post writes it only when the machine file lists option 2.\n  - `g62_t_max_um`: the largest documented T for each control and NC software (10 mm or 99999.999 mm; 0 = no cycle 32). Where a manual states no range, the post uses 10 mm, the narrowest documented range.\n- The post refuses by name:\n  - a T above the range of the control;\n  - a positive T that rounds to `T0` (the control reads T 0 as the tolerance of the machine builder);\n  - smoothing on a stated control without cycle 32 (TNC 410).\n- Where `P01` is not written and the ask is rough, the post writes T only and gives a counted warning.\n- A machine with no controller identity keeps the TNC 640 34059x-07 level of this post: `P01` is written.\n- The sources and the dropped options are in `docs/decisions/4226-g62-smoothing.md`.\n\n## Fehlmann Picomax 55 (iTNC 530, NC 340490-03)\n\nThe output is byte-identical: `G62 T<tol>`. The machine file lists no installed options, and the iTNC 530 340 49x-03 ISO manual permits `P01`/`P02` only with option 2. The research does not prove that the current output is wrong for this control. New on this machine: a rough ask gives a warning, and a T above 10 mm is refused.\n\n## What posts now (examples)\n\n| Machine | Ask | Block |\n|---|---|---|\n| no controller identity, or TNC 640 340595-08 | 0.02 mm finish | `G62 T0.02 P01 0 P02 0` |\n| same | 0.1 mm rough | `G62 T0.1 P01 1 P02 0` |\n| Picomax 55 (no options listed) | 0.02 mm finish or rough | `G62 T0.02` (rough: warning) |\n| iTNC 530 340490-03 with option 2 listed | 0.1 mm rough | `G62 T0.1 P01 1 P02 0` |\n| TNC 430 280476-01 | 0.1 mm rough | `G62 T0.1` (warning) |\n| TNC 640 340595-08 | 10.001 mm | refused: `smoothing tolerance T10.001 mm is above the largest T of TNC 640 NC 340595-08 (profile tnc640-c) (10 mm)` |\n| TNC 410 286060-01 | 0.02 mm | refused: `has no tolerance cycle (cycle 32 / G62)` |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post` `script_heidenhain`:\n  - `picomax::g62::picomax_g62_stays_t_only_without_option_2`\n  - `picomax::g62::g62_writes_the_finish_or_rough_mode_where_the_control_takes_it`\n  - `picomax::g62::g62_refuses_a_t_outside_the_documented_range_by_name`\n- `camcraft-post` lib: `post::heidenhain_dialect::tests::g62_mode_and_t_range_boundaries`, and the updated `the_picomax_control_is_the_itnc_49x_profile` and `the_script_value_names_the_flags_or_the_refusal`.\n- `camcraft-app` `smoothing`: `each_dialect_writes_its_words_and_undoes_them_at_the_section_end` now asserts `P01 0` / `P01 1` for Heidenhain. `off_is_byte_identical_and_writes_no_smoothing_word` holds: a program with no smoothing posts as before.\n- No recorded golden carries smoothing, so no golden changed.\n\n## Gate results\n\nHead `85137b87a`, merged with `origin/main` `2f766c307` for the runs.\n\n- winbuild lane (`camcraft-post`, trial-merge head `2173bc0db`), log `gate-4226-85137b8-post.log`:\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib heidenhain`: 14 passed.\n  - `script_heidenhain` 19 passed, `heidenhain_cycles` 24, `heidenhain_arc_centre` 2, `heidenhain_block_form` 6, `script_heidenhain_klartext` 29.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Mac lane (`--needs app --pool`, head `85137b87a`), log `gate-4226-85137b8-app.log`:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 299 steps, 299 ok, 0 failed. The plan includes `post lib`, the `script_heidenhain` and `script_heidenhain_klartext` post suites, and the app suites `smoothing` and `example_catalog`.\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog --test example_catalog_adaptive --test example_catalog_edge_work`: all pass.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`): not run. The Mac lane was in use by other workers. The reviewer runs it.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on a real control. The option 2 rule for the Picomax comes from the manual only.\n- The Klartext post (`heidenhain-klartext.cps`) still refuses smoothing. `CYCL DEF 32.2 HSC-MODE` can use the same flag later.\n\n## Merge note\n\nThe resolver file `heidenhain_profiles.rs` gets two new fields in `Flags` and split rows (iTNC 530 34049x, TNC 320 77185x, TNC 620 81760x, TNC 640 34059x-07..09). A parallel PR that adds a flag to `Flags` will touch the same struct and the Picomax test literal.\n\nChangelog: Heidenhain DIN/ISO post: G62 now writes the finish or rough filter mode (P01) where the control takes it, and refuses a tolerance T outside the documented range of the control.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4226\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
